SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Nuts & Bolts of Podcasting
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260303T213000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260303T223000Z
UID:69837a6d8b29ea2800cdd35c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to make a podcast! Amanda Cupido\, award-winning po
 dcast producer\, university instructor\, former TPL Innovator in Residence
 \, and author of\nLet's Talk Podcasting\n\, walks you through everything 
 you need to know before you start recording.\nThese are the tricks that ca
 n truly make a podcast shine. We’ll cover the importance of choosing a f
 ormat\, creating a compelling script and how to engage listeners through a
  strong call to action. If you are thinking about starting a podcast\, or 
 are interested in taking your show to the next level\, this is for you.\nT
 his program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place
  for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always
  available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch
  with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd Floor Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69837a6d8b29ea2800cdd35c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
