X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto": "https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/313212947/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ms_reactor
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_313212947@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260303T215745Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260304T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260304T120000
SUMMARY:End-to-End Model Development on Microsoft Foundry
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn this session\, we explore the en
 d-to-end journey of designing and developing AI solutions with Microsoft F
 oundry models. The session is structured around four key phases of the mod
 el development journey.\n\nWe begin with Model Understanding\, where you d
 iscover the Foundry model catalog and build intuition around core model ca
 pabilities. Next is Model Selection\, focusing on how to choose the right 
 model for a given use case using benchmarks\, evaluations\, and leaderboar
 ds. We then move into Model Customization\, covering how models can be ada
 pted through techniques such as context engineering\, fine‑tuning\, and 
 compression to better meet application needs. Finally\, we close with Mode
 l Observability\, highlighting how evaluations\, tracing\, and monitoring 
 help ensure models behave safely\, reliably\, and effectively at scale.\n\
 n-----------------------------------------------\n[The Java-Script AI Buil
 d-a-thon](https://aka.ms/JSAIBuildathon)\n\n📌 This session is a part of
  a series! Learn more [here](https://developer.microsoft.com/reactor/serie
 s/S-1628/?wt.mc_id=meetup_S-1628_webpage_reactor)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3132
 12947/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260205T005756Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260205T005756Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
