BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Botanical Garden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-special-occasion-flowers-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_botanical
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260304T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260325T210000
DTSTAMP:20260303T164456
CREATED:20251205T182513Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251222T172501Z
UID:10001895-1772647200-1774472400@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Floral Design Program: Special Occasion Flowers
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to design and create your own spectacular bouquets\, centerpieces\, and more! Create floral designs for special occasions such as heart-shaped bouquets for Valentine’s day\, boutonnieres\, corsages\, centerpieces for weddings\, and cake toppers for birthdays\, graduations\, and anniversaries. Prerequisites: Classic Design Fundamentals I & II. Learn more about our Certificate in Floral Design\n \nWednesdays\, March 4\, 11\, 18\, 25\, 6 to 9 p.m. (Snow date: Thursday\, March 2)\n\nPublic $240\, Members $190 (plus applicable taxes and fees) \nRegistration deadline: Friday\, February 27\, 2026 at 12:00 PM. \nPlease note: Course fees do not include flowers or supplies. Students are encouraged to find a local flower shop or grocery store to purchase their flowers. A materials list will be e-mailed prior to the start of each class. \n\n\n\nAbout Margaret Taylor\nFor 25 years\, Margaret’s passion for flowers has led her to exhibit\, judge\, demonstrate and teach floral design in Canada and abroad. A recipient of many awards\, Margaret’s accolades include three Canada Blooms’ Founder’s Gold Cups for Best in Show. Margaret has also won Best in Show on three occasions at the provincial triennial show and as a result\, has been chosen to represent Canada in two world shows. It was her greatest honour to exhibit for Canada both in Boston and in India. \nMargaret is currently a floral design judge accredited by the Garden Clubs of Ontario\, a horticultural judge accredited by the Royal Botanical Gardens and a rose judge accredited by the Canadian Rose Society. Margaret is also a Sogetsu Ikebana teacher and exhibitor. She is the current Director of the Toronto Sogetsu Chapter and on the board of the Japanese Garden Club as the Ikebana Coordinator. Much lauded for her design acumen by the horticultural community\, she is a past president of the Garden Club of Toronto and is a coordinator of floral design studies at Toronto Botanical Garden. \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member! \nAdditional Program Information\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program\, please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-special-occasion-flowers-2/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Avenue East\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Floral Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/28285cf3c55886f23c210752e4466074.jpg
END:VEVENT
