SUMMARY:The Music of the Beatles - A Symphonic Experience (St Andrew Stati
 on)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nOn **Wednesday March 4th** **join me for R
 EVOLUTION: The Music of the Beatles - A Symphonic Experience**. Relive the
  revolutionary music of the Fab Four with GRAMMY ® Award winner Jeff Tyzi
 k’s new arrangements\, transcribed directly from the original master rec
 ordings at Abbey Road. Accompanied by hundreds of rare and unseen photos f
 rom the archives of The Beatles’ official fan magazine *The Beatles Book
 \, REVOLUTION: The Music of The Beatles—A Symphonic Experience* will tak
 e you on a magical mystery tour with top hits like “Ticket to Ride”\, 
 “Penny Lane”\, “All You Need Is Love”\, “Here Comes the Sun”\,
  and “Hey Jude”. As a subscriber\, I can buy additional seats at the s
 ubscriber price for attendees. My seat is Orchestra Right B35. **Purchase 
 your tickets for REVOLUTION: The Music of the Beatles - A Symphonic Experi
 ence on Wednesday March 4th at 7:30pm**.\n\n**COST**\nRegular: $85 - 170 i
 ncludes taxes and fees\n\nRush: A limited number of tickets may go on sale
  at 1pm online\, over the phone\, or in-person at Roy Thomson Hall. Limit 
 2 per person based on availability.\n\nMeetup fee: $5\n\nTicket Policy: Sa
 les are final and non-refundable.\n\n***\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **Simply R
 SVP Yes\, [purchase](https://my.tso.ca/3649/3717) your ticket and post you
 r seat number and I will move you to attending.**\n* If you plan to buy RU
 SH\, please state that in your RSVP\, so I can include you in the reminder
  and we can meet you.\n* RSVPs close 2 days prior\, and cancellations afte
 r will result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n* A reminder wil
 l go out the day before with my cell and details when to meet\, etc.\n\n
 ‐‐----‐----‐‐-------------‐-----------\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Mee
 t me at 7pm** **at Roy Thomson Hall at 60 Simcoe St.\, inside the southern
 -most double set of glass doors\, after scanning your tickets. We will sta
 rt the night with a drink.**\n\n**Start time: 7:30pm**\nLength: 2 hours (i
 ncludes intermission)\n\nEnjoy and please post your Comments after!
