SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260303T215745Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260305T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260305T080000
SUMMARY:Tools\, MCP and Agents with LangChain4j
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nMove from "text generator" to "acti
 on taker." You'll expose Java methods as tools using @Tool annotations and
  watch the AI chain them automatically with the ReAct pattern. Then you'll
  explore Model Context Protocol (MCP)—an open standard for AI-to-tool co
 mmunication—and build a Supervisor Agent that dynamically orchestrates s
 ub-agents to read files\, analyze content\, and summarize results\n\nPre-r
 equisites:\nCheck out the LangChain4j beginners series: https://aka.ms/lan
 gchain4j-for-beginners\nSign up for an Azure free trial: https://aka.ms/Az
 ureFreeTrialDevRelAll
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3122
 98303/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20251204T151438Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251204T151438Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Botanical Garden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/nature-of-chi-tai-chi-qigong-at-the-garden-7-sessions/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_botanical
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260305T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260416T113000
DTSTAMP:20260303T164456
CREATED:20260106T204933Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260206T193035Z
UID:10001908-1772699400-1776339000@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Nature of Chi: Tai Chi & Qigong at the Garden (7 sessions)
DESCRIPTION:Join us Thursday mornings for Tai Chi and Qigong at the Garden!\n\n\n“CHI” is the universal life force that runs through our bodies. Routine practice of Tai Chi & Qigong can help cultivate our internal energy flow. “NATURE OF CHI ”combines seasonal Tai Chi & Qigong to help restore\, regulate and awaken our natural body functions. Classes will include warm ups\, breath work\, a variety of Tai Chi & Qigong movements that connect to the 5 elements\, and a short guided meditation to help relax\, calm and balance mind\, body & spirit. “NATURE OF CHI” Tai Chi is suitable for all age groups\, fitness levels\, and does not require any previous Tai Chi or Qigong experience. \nClasses will be held indoors for the Winter session looking outdoors from the beautiful & spacious Garden Hall. \nProgram Schedule: Thursdays\, March 5-April 16\, 2026 from 8:30 to 9:30 a.m. (7 sessions). \nRegistration: Public $107\, TBG Member $84 (plus applicable taxes and fees) \nAbout David Leopold \nSifu David Leopold has been practicing\, studying\, researching and teaching martial and healing arts since 1994. \nIn 1999\, Sifu David achieved his black belt in Shaolin Kung Fu. Since 1999\, Sifu David has received numerous certifications in Tachi had and weapon forms and seven Qigong routines. In 2009\, Sifu David received his Usui Reiki master certification from the Naturopathic School of Medicine in Toronto. \nIn 2012\, Sifu David travelled to China to compete in the International Wushi Competition in Shanghai. He brought home 2 gold and a bronze medal. \nBy combining all these modalities and experiences\, Sifu David brings a unique style of teaching that includes technique\, philosophy and practicality. Sify David’s approach to teaching is relaxed and he believes Taichi and Qigong practice should be useful in everyday life and enjoyable to do. \nSifu David has a passion for martial and healing arts. His holistic approach to wellness includes physical\, emotional\, spiritual and nutritional well being. Sifu David continues to improve his skills as a practitioner\, teacher/ mentor\, and hopes to teach for the rest of his life. \nSifu David’s words of wisdom: \n“To be a master of what you do\, you must first be a master unto yourself.” \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member! \nAdditional Program Information \n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/nature-of-chi-tai-chi-qigong-at-the-garden-7-sessions/
LOCATION:ON
CATEGORIES:Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/a93d55efa867d63a8cf6ac705f36c718.jpg
END:VEVENT
