SUMMARY:Studio Portrait Perfection lighting workshop w Lilli F
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Photography Group\n## Time & Location\n\nMar 05\, 
 2026\, 7:00 PM – 10:00 PM\nRevprint Studio 205 \, 146 Thirtieth St\, Eto
 bicoke\, ON M8W 3C4\, Canada\n\n## About the event\n\n### **Studio Portrai
 t Lighting Workshop**\n\n**Date:** Thursday\, March 5th 2026\n**Time:** 7:
 00 PM – 10:00 PM\n**Instructor:** *Phil Sutherland* – Elinchrom Ambass
 ador & Executive Director\, West Toronto Photography Group\nModel Lilli F 
 - gallery of images from previous workshop\n![](https://static.wixstatic.c
 om/media/1eaf19_e3c6cd31779841cd8c1db56c456538d0~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1686\,h
 _1000\,fp_0.50_0.50\,q_90/1eaf19_e3c6cd31779841cd8c1db56c456538d0~mv2.webp
 )\n![](https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19_d1c7d94c7d644d50ad0382a9d
 f104150~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1280\,h_759\,fp_0.50_0.50\,q_90/1eaf19_d1c7d94c7
 d644d50ad0382a9df104150~mv2.webp)\n![](https://static.wixstatic.com/media/
 1eaf19_596cac5757304458ba116c59d7a27ec0~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1524\,h_904\,fp_
 0.50_0.50\,q_90/1eaf19_596cac5757304458ba116c59d7a27ec0~mv2.webp)\n![](htt
 ps://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19_6ac151a9cac24a34a3ae766fffa9aeda~mv
 2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1686\,h_1000\,fp_0.50_0.50\,q_90/1eaf19_6ac151a9cac24a34a3
 ae766fffa9aeda~mv2.webp)\n![](https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1eaf19_50
 46bc6311fb483e83c6fa540e454065~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1686\,h_1000\,fp_0.50_0.5
 0\,q_90/1eaf19_5046bc6311fb483e83c6fa540e454065~mv2.webp)\n**Lighting Equi
 pment:** Provided by **Elinchrom**\n**Location:** Revprint Studio 205 - 14
 6 Thirtierth street unit 205\n**Workshop Size:** Limited to **6 participan
 ts**\n\n#### **Workshop Overview**\n\nJoin us for a fun and informative **
 Portrait Perfection photography lighting and shooting workshop** designed 
 to help you build skills and portfolio images and technical skills in the 
 art of portrait lighting. Whether you’re new to studio photography or lo
 oking to refine your lighting technique\, this hands-on session will guide
  you through essential tools\, setups\, and creative lighting approaches.\
 nThis **three-hour\, small-group workshop** ensures plenty of individual a
 ttention\, shooting time\, and opportunities to ask questions.\n\n#### **W
 hat You’ll Learn**\n\n1. **Studio Gear** A detailed overview of lighting
  equipment\, modifiers\, and how we will use them for each lighting set up
  we build as a group ..\n2. **Studio Design & Setup**Understand how to pla
 n and use studio space efficiently for portrait sessions.\n3. **Modifiers 
 & Light Quality** Explore how different modifiers affect your images as we
  utilize the Rotolaux modifiers from Elinchrom in studio.\n4. **Building a
  Lighting Setup** As a group we will step-by-step construct professional p
 ortrait lighting setups using Elinchrom lights and modifiers.\n5. **Hands-
 On Shooting Practice** Photograph our model Lilli in **multiple lighting s
 etups that create strong and elegant lighting** —each participant will h
 ave one-on-one shooting time and instructor feedback. You will get some st
 unning images for your portfolio from the small group 3 hour portrait perf
 ection lighting workshop\n\n#### **Who Should Attend**\n\nThis workshop is
  ideal for photographers of all skill levels who want to:\n\n* Learn or re
 fresh the fundamentals of portrait and studio lighting or pick up a few ne
 w tricks\n* Get hands-on experience with professional lighting equipment f
 rom Elinchrom\n* Practice creating and refining lighting setups that you c
 an use to WOW clients\n* Build confidence shooting portraits in a studio e
 nvironment while updating your portfolio\n\n#### **What to Bring**\n\n* A 
 **DSLR or mirrorless camera** with a working hot-shoe\n* **Fresh batteries
 ** and **formatted memory cards**\n* Your **favourite lens** (anything bet
 ween 10mm–200mm works great)\n* Curiosity\, creativity\, and your passio
 n for photography!\n\n#### **What’s Included**\n\n* Professional instruc
 tion and lighting gear provided by **Elinchrom**\n* Access to a variety of
  light modifiers: reflectors\, umbrellas\, softboxes\, grids\, snoots\, an
 d beauty dishes\n* A safe\, supportive\, and professional environment to l
 earn and network\n* Dedicated time with the model for individual shooting 
 opportunities\n\n\\*\\*Time is money\, and we value yours.\\*\\*That’s w
 hy we keep our workshops efficient\, informative\, and fun—so you leave 
 inspired\, informed\, and ready to light your next portrait session like a
  pro.
