SUMMARY:Seussical: The Musical
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260306T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260314T190000
UID:58a124d994d51545c01ff3caa49ed169@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:A vibrant stage adaptation that weaves together iconic charact
 ers and stories from the world of Dr. Seuss.\n\nHorton the Elephant stumbl
 es upon a tiny speck of dust containing an entire community\, the Whos of 
 Who-ville. When he alone hears their call for help\, Horton makes a bold p
 romise to protect them\, even as doubt spreads and he faces mounting dange
 r. Along the way\, Gertrude McFuzz struggles to find her confidence\, Jojo
  searches for belonging\, and The Cat in the Hat leads us through a world 
 where imagination challenges reality and compassion changes everything.\n\
 nAt its heart\, Seussical is a story about loyalty\, self-discovery\, and 
 standing up for others\, even when you’re the only one who believes.\n\n
 This is Hillcrest Village Community Players' milestone fifth season show f
 eaturing local talent from across the city. You don't want to miss this!\n
 \nCategories: Family/Children\, Live Performances\, Theatre\nPrice: 41.00
LOCATION:St. Matthew's United Church\, 729 St Clair Ave W\, Toronto\, ON\,
  M6C 1B2
URL:https://www.hillcrestvillageplayers.ca/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
