SUMMARY:50% off SOME LIKE IT HOT Tony & Grammy Award Winner (Dundas Stn.)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**Note: Black Friday Sale up to 34% off en
 ded Mon. Dec. 1\, 2025 at 11:59pm EST.**\n\nOn **Friday March 6th\,** **se
 e SOME LIKE IT HOT\, 4-time Tony Award Winner plus Grammy Award Winner of 
 Best Theatre Musical Album. SOME LIKE IT HOT** is “a super-sized\, all-o
 ut song-and-dance spectacular!” – *The New York Times.* *Deadline* cal
 ls it “a tap-dancing\, razzle-dazzling embrace of everything you love ab
 out musical theatre.” Set in Chicago when Prohibition has everyone thirs
 ty for a little excitement\, **SOME LIKE IT HOT** is the “glorious\, big
 \, high-kicking” story of two musicians forced to flee the Windy City af
 ter witnessing a mob hit. With gangsters hot on their heels\, they catch a
  cross-country train for the life-chasing\, life-changing trip of a lifeti
 me.. My seat is Orchestra S25. **Purchase Some Like It Hot on Friday March
  6th at 7:30pm.**\n\n**COST**\nRegular Cost: $49/ 89/ 109/ 139/ 159/ 225 +
  service fees\n\n**Discounted Cost: 50% off** + service fees (discount cod
 e is embedded in the Purchase link below. If it doesn't work\, please reac
 h out to me.)\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n**Ticket Policy**: All sales 
 are final\, no refunds or exchanges.\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes** *
 *(everyone goes on the waitlist until they post their seat number)**\n* **
 [Purchase](https://www.mirvish.com/shows/some-like-it-hot)** **your own ti
 cket and select the March 6th date**\, post your seat number and I will mo
 ve you to going.\n\nA reminder will be sent the day before with my cell an
 d reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRSVPs close 2 days prior and
  the Waitlist will be removed at that time. Cancellations will result in a
  No Show and impact future attendance.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for t
 he Show at: 7:10pm inside the CAA Ed Mirvish Theatre at 244 Victoria St.**
 \, on the ground floor **to the right side after scanning your tickets.**\
 n\n**Start: 7:30pm**\n\nLength: 2 hours 40 mins (incl. intermission)\n\nAf
 ter: meet at the same spot to chat about the show.\n\nEnjoy and please pos
 t your comments in the Event after.
