SUMMARY:Arturo O'Farrill Afro-Latin Jazz Ensemble
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T200000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260307T200000
UID:80f567cd1f5bf8e2583c003b0ed0fca9@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:The multi-Grammy Award-winning pianist dazzles as he honours D
 izzy Gillespie and Charlie Parker with his band\, continuing his father Ch
 ico O’Farrill’s legacy of composing and arranging for these jazz icons
 .\n\nArturo O’Farrill\, pianist\, composer\, and educator\, was born in 
 Mexico and grew up in New York City. His professional career began with th
 e Carla Bley Band and continued as a solo performer with a wide spectrum o
 f artists including Dizzy Gillespie\, Lester Bowie\, Wynton Marsalis\, and
  Harry Belafonte. \n\nHis powerful piece “Three Revolutions” from the 
 album "Familia: Tribute to Bebo & Chico" won the 2018 Grammy Award for Bes
 t Instrumental Composition. Most recently\, in February of 2023\, Arturo w
 as awarded his eighth Grammy for the album "Fandango at the Wall in New Yo
 rk".\n\nAfter the concert\, enjoy a beverage and more music.\n\nCategories
 : Arts/Exhibits\, Live Performances\, Music
LOCATION:Koerner Hall\, Royal Conservatory of Music\, 273 Bloor St W\, Tor
 onto\, ON\, M5S 1W2
URL:https://www.rcmusic.com/events-and-performances/arturo-ofarrill-octet
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
