BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-centres-galleries/assembly-hall/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Bad Indians Book Club by Patty Krawec - By the Lake Book Club
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260310T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260310T190000
UID:a83df210a385ec45914aa94e9206ee31@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Bad Indians Book Club\, by Anishinaabe and Ukrainian writer Pa
 tty Krawec\, is a bold exploration of Indigenous literature and the storie
 s that challenge colonial narratives. Emerging from a year-long reading jo
 urney\, Krawec blends memoir\, cultural critique\, and storytelling to exa
 mine works by marginalized voices and their power to reshape identity and 
 belonging. Interwoven with the figure of Deer Woman\, this book invites re
 aders to the edges of worlds waiting to be born. Praised with a Booklist s
 tarred review\, it offers a potent call to rethink the stories we inherit.
 \n\nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to 
 December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in
 -person event features readings\, discussions\, Q&A\, book signings and AS
 L interpretation\, while virtual sessions include live subtitles and audio
  access.\nCategories: Literary
LOCATION:Assembly Hall\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicoke\, ON\,
  M8V 4B6
URL:https://www.toronto.ca/explore-enjoy/history-art-culture/cultural-cent
 res-galleries/assembly-hall/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
