SUMMARY:Philosophy Undergraduate Research Conference
DESCRIPTION:It’s that time of year again! Join us for exciting debates and new ideas in undergraduate philosophy scholarship at the 2026 Undergraduate Philosophy Research Conference. Expect a full day of insight\, discussion\, and community. \nThis year’s keynote speaker is Arianna Falbo [URL: https://www.torontomu.ca/philosophy/faculty-staff/arianna-falbo/] (TMU)\, who will be speaking at 3:30 PM on Friday March 13\, 2026. Dr. Falbo’s research focuses on inquiry\, with areas of expertise in epistemology\, feminist and social philosophy\, and philosophy of language. \nPlease check back soon for a fuller event schedule.
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/philosophy-undergraduate-conference/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:St. George,Undergraduate
