BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://national.ballet.ca/productions/2526/pinocchio/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Pinocchio
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260313T193000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260322T140000
UID:cfdbcabb9367c0b270a567caffda3dc6@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Olivier Award-winning director and choreographer Will Tuckett 
 created Pinocchio for The National Ballet of Canada in 2017\, based on the
  19th-century tale about a wooden puppet who longs to be real. \n\nThe hea
 rt of that story is love\, as the fatherly Geppetto guides Pinocchio’s u
 nderstanding of what it means to be human. Tuckett balances the moral aspe
 cts of the original story with heartwarming characters\, magical stage eff
 ects and playful Canadiana\, making Pinocchio a delightful experience for 
 audiences of all ages.\n\nCategories: Dance\, Live Performances
LOCATION:Four Seasons Centre for the Performing Arts\, 145 Queen St W\, To
 ronto\, ON\, M5H 4G1
URL:https://national.ballet.ca/productions/2526/pinocchio/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
