SUMMARY:Garden Tune-Up: Winter Pruning Made Simple
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to learn everything you need to know about pruning this winter!\n\n\nJoin TBG’s Lead Horticulturist Leslie Hockley\, as she demonstrates winter pruning practices for shrubs\, trees and vines. The session will begin with an indoor lecture-style presentation covering techniques and visual cues for determining when and how to prune. Afterwards\, Leslie will take participants on a guided tour through the gardens and demonstrate the techniques discussed in the lecture. Please dress according to the weather conditions. \nSaturday\, March 14\, 10 a.m. to 12 p.m.Public $25\, TBG Members $20 (plus applicable taxes and fees). \nAbout Leslie Hockley\nTBG’s Lead Horticulturist\, Leslie Hockley is passionate about all things public gardens. Before joining TBG in 2023\, Leslie worked for several botanical gardens in North America in garden maintenance\, design\, tree care and plant records roles. She is a Red Seal Endorsed Horticulturist and has studied horticulture at Humber College and the Niagara Parks Commission School of Horticulture. \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member ! \nAdditional Program Information\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/garden-tune-up-winter-pruning-made-simple/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Avenue East\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Gardening
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/e7a51124ff08b7d9aedfcbc61f0bfe75.jpg
END:VEVENT
