X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardiner Museum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/march-break-camp-all-about-clay-ages-6-8-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardiner_museum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260316T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260320T120000
DTSTAMP:20260303T164537
CREATED:20260108T174400Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260211T233141Z
UID:141210-1773651600-1774008000@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:March Break Camp: All About Clay (Ages 6 - 8)
DESCRIPTION:March Break Camp: All About Clay (Ages 6 – 8)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Monday March 16 – Friday March 20\, 2026\n9:00 am – 12:o0 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Join us for a week of clay and creativity this March Break! Kids 6 – 8 will discover the stages of making pottery—from sculpting and glazing to firing—tapping into their creativity to create original ceramic sculptures using clay and other modelling materials. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Camp Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \n\n\n\n\nDay 1: Intro to hand building with clay\nDay 2: Gallery exploration and hand building in the studio\nDay 3: Intro to glazing\nDay 4: Gallery exploration and using other sculpting materials\nDay 5: Complete projects and artwork showcase\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $212.50\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $250\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \n\n\n\n\nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $30 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase kids camps at the discounted rate for membership card holders’ children and grandchildren. \n\n\n\n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/march-break-camp-all-about-clay-ages-6-8-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Kids Camps
