BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardiner Museum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/stoneware-intermediate-spring-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardiner_museum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260331T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260519T163000
DTSTAMP:20260303T164537
CREATED:20260211T162717Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260216T202311Z
UID:142055-1774963800-1779208200@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Stoneware (Intermediate)
DESCRIPTION:Stoneware (Intermediate)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Tuesdays March 31 to May 19\, 2026\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 18+ \nDevelop your skills in wheel throwing\, hand building\, glazing\, texturing\, and more using stoneware clay. This free-form or open studio style class will focus on independent experimentation and is designed for students with previous experience working with clay. \nThis class includes a 10kg bag of stoneware clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional bags of clay can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $434\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $510\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: March 31\, April 7\, 14\, 21\, 28\, May 5\, 12\, 19 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Mohammad Tabesh\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Mohammad Tabesh is a Toronto-based multidisciplinary artist whose work delves into the complexities of the human experience\, resistance\, and social change. Across various mediums\, including writing\, printmaking\, multimedia\, and sculpture\, Mohammad strives to convey deeply human and universal stories. His work has been recognized with several Canada Council for the Arts grants and an Access Copyright Foundation grant. Mohammad earned his BFA from OCAD University and was honoured as the recipient of the Sculpture and Installation Medal in 2020. In 2022\, he was accepted as an Artist-in-Residence for ceramics at Harbourfront Centre. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/stoneware-intermediate-spring-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Adult-Class-Thumbnail-7.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardiner Museum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-wheel-throwing-combo-beginner-spring-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardiner_museum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260331T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T163000
DTSTAMP:20260303T164537
CREATED:20260211T162717Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260216T202719Z
UID:142057-1774963800-1779813000@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Hand Building and Wheel Throwing Combo (Beginner)
DESCRIPTION:Hand Building and Wheel Throwing Combo (Beginner)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Tuesdays March 31 to May 26\, 2026\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 18+ \nStart by learning the basic techniques of hand building—pinch\, coil\, and slab building—to create functional and sculptural wares. You’ll also learn the fundamentals of creating and finishing pieces on the pottery wheel. This 8-week class is designed for beginners. \nThis class includes a 10kg bag of clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional bags of clay can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $412\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $485\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: March 31\, April 14\, 21\, 28\, May 5\, 12\, 19\, 26\nNo class April 7 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nWeek 1: Learn to pinch\, coil\, and roll slabs to create functional or sculptural works\, with a focus on cylinders and cups\nWeek 2: Learn the fundamental of throwing a cylinder on the wheel\nWeek 3: Trim your wheel pieces and learn to make attachments such as handles\nWeek 4: Continue to work on hand-building techniques to create bowls and trays\nLearn to make a bowl on the wheel\nWeek 5: Review trimming and trim a bowl on the wheel\nContinue to hand build or make new pieces on the wheel\nWeek 6: Learn decoration techniques for hand-built and wheel pieces\nWeek 7: Continue works in progress\nWeek 8: Glaze and complete works\n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Chloe Begg\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Chloe Begg is an educator and emerging artist living in Toronto/Tkaronto. After receiving an M.Sc. in Sustainable Development and working for five years in the solar industry\, Chloe pivoted to complete a certificate in Ceramic Arts from the Haliburton School of Art and Design in 2022. In early 2024\, Chloe attended the Banff Centre for Arts as an emerging artist in residence. In the summer of 2024 Chloe participated in the City of Toronto’s Public Art Mentorship program\, which will culminate in a six-month installation at the Toronto Sculpture Garden in April 2026 focusing on play and interactivity. In 2025\, Chloe participated in the DesignTO Festival with a solo exhibition\, The Artist Project in Toronto\, and group shows across Ontario. Chloe is currently working with mentors through the Cohorts.Art and FUSION mentorship programs to further work which focuses on connection\, belonging\, and identity. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-wheel-throwing-combo-beginner-spring-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Adult-Class-Thumbnail-1.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
