X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260402T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260514T163000
DTSTAMP:20260303T164537
CREATED:20260211T162633Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260223T171011Z
UID:142073-1775136600-1778776200@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Coasters\, Trivets\, and Magnets: Stoneware (All Levels)
DESCRIPTION:Coasters\, Trivets\, and Magnets: Stoneware (All Levels)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Thursdays April 2 to May 14\, 2026\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 18+ \nDiscover practical ways to work with ceramic tiles in this stoneware class. Use traditional hand-building techniques to create a set of coasters\, a large trivet\, and decorative magnets while learning all the essential tile-making techniques\, including how to dry tiles flat to prevent warping as well as underglazing and glazing. You’ll come away with a collection of handmade items perfect for your home or to give as gifts. This 6-week class is designed for all levels. \nThis class includes access to one 5kg bag of stoneware clay\, as well as glazes and underglazes. Additional bags of clay can be purchased for $18 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $268\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $315\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: April 2\, 9\, 16\, 30\, May 7\, May 14\nNo class on April 23 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nWeek 1: Design time and introduction to tile making and hand building\nLearn proper drying techniques to keep tiles flat and warp-free\nWeek 2: Complete coaster set\nBegin trivets\nWeek 3: Complete trivets\nLearn about glazing techniques\nWeek 4: Make magnet set\nWeek 5: Complete all glazing and prepare pieces for once-firing\nWeek 6: Final class show and pick up of items\nTour the Galleries\n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Meg Leslie\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Meg Leslie is a Canadian mosaic and ceramic artist. Her work is deeply rooted in nature\, storytelling\, and community. With a background in interior design and a Master Naturalist certificate\, she brings a layered approach to her art\, blending structural and organic\, personal and ecological. Her practice has evolved from large-scale pique assiette public mosaic installations to more intimate explorations in handmade porcelain tiles. Over the past decade\, she has led numerous community art projects\, workshops\, and creative initiatives across Ontario. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/coasters-trivets-and-magnets-stoneware-all-levels-spring-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
