BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a0c4abcbf6405d3568bda8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Teen Quiet Study
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T230000Z
UID:69a0c4abcbf6405d3568bda8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you looking for a quiet space to study after school? Join 
 our quiet study hall at Locke's program room every Thursday for individual
  or group study. Tables and chairs are provided\, as well as a variety of
  materials to take study breaks.\nThis is a drop-in program for Teens\, a
 nd space is limited.
LOCATION:Locke\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a0c4abcbf6405d3568bda8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711f61c967cb4120833b67"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Crafty Thursdays
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T220000Z
UID:69711f61c967cb4120833b67@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub every Thursday for a series of crafti
 ng activities like painting\, clay sculpting\, sewing and embroidery\, res
 in art\, jewelry making\, perler beads\, block printing\, and more! Check 
 tpl.ca or our monthly calendar for the activity of the week. All material
 s provided.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a w
 elcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful st
 aff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Dr
 op by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711f61c967cb4120833b67
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698b5ac22a787a47a5e6fcf9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Club: The Play's the Thing! - Theatre Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T210000Z
UID:698b5ac22a787a47a5e6fcf9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Kids take ownership of every element of creating their very ow
 n play or puppet show\, from set decoration to costume or puppet making to
  script writing to performance. Incorporating movement activities\, group 
 collaboration\, and artistic expression\, this program can help children w
 ith confidence and allows them to work to their individual strengths. For 
 children 6-12 years.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informa
 tion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pub
 lic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wi
 ll only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluati
 on. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direct
 ed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge 
 Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698b5ac22a787a47a5e6fcf9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6997ab248d5e2d09336056ae"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Japanese fruit sandwiches\, with Chef Yumiko Kobayashi
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T210000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T220000Z
UID:6997ab248d5e2d09336056ae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Chef Yumiko Kobayashi will provide a brief cultural history ab
 out "Furutsu Sandos"\, or Japanese fruit sandwiches\, then lead a hands-on
  demonstration and workshop to make "Furutsu Sandos” consisting of fresh
  fruit fillings\, bread and whipping cream\n.Food allergy notice: Please b
 e aware that food will be used in this program that contains gluten and da
 iry.  Certain food ingredients may cause allergic reactions in some people
 . ​
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6997ab248d5e2d09336056ae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69975824b0595799c09dfab8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Introduction to 3D Printing
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T233000Z
UID:69975824b0595799c09dfab8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how 3D printers work and how you can print at the Toront
 o Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This class includes hands-on
  instruction with Prusa Slicer\, the software used to prepare your 3D obje
 ct file for printing on a Prusa MK3S+ 3D printer.\nNote: Customers are no 
 longer required to attend a mandatory 3D printing class prior to using a 3
 D printer at the Toronto Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This 
 class is for those who are interested in learning more about 3D printing a
 nd how to use the Prusa software.\nRegistration is required.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Basement Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69975824b0595799c09dfab8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a07"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Throwback Thursdays: Great Movies on the Big Screen
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260403T000000Z
UID:699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a07@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a radical retro rewind projected on the big s
 creen. Whether you're a first-time viewer or long-time fan\, these movies 
 are sure to please.\nFebruary 26: If Beale Street Could Talk (2018\, 14A)
 \nMarch 5: The Social Network (2010\, PG)\nMarch 12: Steve Jobs (2015\, R
 )\nMarch 19: Michael Clayton (2007\, 14A)\nMarch 26: Ocean’s Twelve (2
 004\, PG)\nAll are welcome. Drop-in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a07
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
