 n play or puppet show\, from set decoration to costume or puppet making to
  script writing to performance. Incorporating movement activities\, group 
 collaboration\, and artistic expression\, this program can help children w
 ith confidence and allows them to work to their individual strengths. For 
 children 6-12 years.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informa
 tion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pub
 lic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wi
 ll only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluati
 on. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direct
 ed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge 
 Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698b5ac22a787a47a5e6fcfa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a091b64a9fd98b7f80bfc0"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Pawsitively Pets
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260409T204500Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260409T213000Z
UID:69a091b64a9fd98b7f80bfc0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pawsitively Pets allows you to explore the wonderful world of 
 animals hands-on through an educational experience.\nDrop-in only\, no reg
 istration necessary.\nProgram held at the Youth Hub.\nThis program is part
  of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after sc
 hool and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\,
  nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\
 nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a091b64a9fd98b7f80bfc0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6967f818b0595799c096625a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Loops\, Swoops and Curlicues Exhibition Tour
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260409T210000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260409T213000Z
UID:6967f818b0595799c096625a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How well can you read handwritten items? This free guided tour
  of\nLoops\, Swoops and Curlicues: A legacy of handwritten history\nwill l
 ead your through hundreds of years of handwritten items from TPL Special C
 ollections.\nCome test your decoding skills as we explore several hundred 
 years of handwritten words.\nRegistration is encouraged\, but not required
 . There is space for drop-in guests. Please meet at the entrance to the TD
  Gallery.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, TD Gallery\, First Floor of Toronto R
 eference Library
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6967f818b0595799c096625a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a08"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Throwback Thursdays: Great Movies on the Big Screen
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260409T220000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260410T000000Z
UID:699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a08@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a radical retro rewind projected on the big s
 creen. Whether you're a first-time viewer or long-time fan\, these movies 
 are sure to please.\nFebruary 26: If Beale Street Could Talk (2018\, 14A)
 \nMarch 5: The Social Network (2010\, PG)\nMarch 12: Steve Jobs (2015\, R
 )\nMarch 19: Michael Clayton (2007\, 14A)\nMarch 26: Ocean’s Twelve (2
 004\, PG)\nAll are welcome. Drop-in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f5cc78b29ea2800d27a08
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
