SUMMARY:Tween Hour- Minute to Win it!
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260421T190000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260421T200000Z
UID:6996340b1e64afd01e5c5b27@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Think you have what it takes to beat the clock? Join us for\nM
 inute to Win It\n\,\na fast-paced\, laugh-out-loud challenge event where p
 articipants compete in a series of 60-second games.\nAges 11-14 years.\nSp
 ace is limited.\nDrop in. First come first serve.
LOCATION:Humberwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6996340b1e64afd01e5c5b27
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/695c3a6cc719ac98c3361768"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696abaf8b0595799c096d200"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260421T193000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260421T203000Z
UID:696abaf8b0595799c096d200@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages\n6-12.\nDrop-in.\nUpcoming Programs:\nMarch 3 - Basketball 
 with Dash\nMarch 10 - DIY Bookmarks\nMarch 17 - No ASC Session - March Bre
 ak program in place\nMarch 24 - Soccer with Sphero\nMarch 31 - Easter Bunn
 y Masks\nSnacks are offered during the After School Club for participants.
 \nFood may contain or have come into contact with common allergens. Ingred
 ient lists will be available. Snacks are generously supported\, in part\, 
 by donors.\nIf you or your child lives with a disability\, and requires an
  accessibility accommodation to participate in this program\, please conta
 ct Accessibility Services by email\, accessibleservices@tpl.ca\, or voicem
 ail\, 416-393-7099\, to make a request. Please contact us at least three w
 eeks in advance.
LOCATION:Jones
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696abaf8b0595799c096d200
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
