SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Mindful Mondays
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260427T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260427T220000Z
UID:69711b91c967cb412083385c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Every Monday\, enjoy a series of stress-relieving mindfulness 
 activities\, crafts\, and games to help ease anxiety and give you a moment
  of Zen. Enjoy mindful colouring sheets\, rainbow scratch art\, mindfulnes
 s card decks\, gratitude journals\, and more. All materials provided.\nThi
 s program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place f
 or teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always a
 vailable. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch w
 ith a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711b91c967cb412083385c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a21806491b809c6f1d05d7"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a21806491b809c6f1d05d6"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Therapy Dog Visits
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260427T200000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260427T203000Z
UID:69a21806491b809c6f1d05d6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for small group visits with therapy dogs. Children wil
 l have an opportunity to read\, listen to stories and engage in therapeuti
 c human-animal interaction. This free program is presented in partnership 
 with One Health Partners.\nChildren who live with a disability\, are neuro
 divergent\, or have experienced medical or other types of trauma are espec
 ially welcome. Suitable for school-aged children ages 6 and up. Siblings a
 ges 6 and up are welcome.\nThere are two 30-minute sessions available: 4-4
 :30 or 4:30-5:00. Please register for one session. Please click on the app
 ropriate program listing to register for that time. There will be limited 
 drop-in spots available on a first come\, first served basis.\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Sensory Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a21806491b809c6f1d05d6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a62ae08d5e2d093362b56e"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Pokémon TCG
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260427T213000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260427T230000Z
UID:69a62ae08d5e2d093362b56e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Grab your cards and ready your decks for a fun-filled Pokémon
  TCG experience! Whether you are a seasoned Trainer or new to the game\, t
 here is always something new to learn and discover. Explore the fascinatin
 g world of Pokémon\, learn about the cards and sets along with learning h
 ow to play the trading card game.\nRegistration is required. For ages 7-1
 2 only (children outside of this age range will not be able to participate
 ).\n*For all registered Children's programs at Malvern\, there is a grace 
 period of 10 minutes. After the first 10 minutes of a program\, spots will
  be given to waiting customers.*\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, 1st Floor Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a62ae08d5e2d093362b56e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
