BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a201c84dacf581ff7e6743"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:History of Generative Music: The Last 50 Years
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260516T180000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260516T200000Z
UID:69a201c84dacf581ff7e6743@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:From the first computer-generated compositions to the AI music
  tools available today\, the past five decades have seen generative music 
 evolve at an extraordinary pace. What began as experiments in university l
 abs has become technology that anyone can access from a laptop or phone.\n
 In this session\, you'll trace the rapid evolution of generative music fro
 m early computer experiments through to modern AI platforms\, discover the
  key innovations that made today's tools possible\, and explore where this
  technology might be heading next.\nDrop-in. No registration required.\nTh
 is program is part of the Innovator in Residence (AI and Music Production)
  program\, which is designed to help beginner and intermediate learners bu
 ild knowledge and creative skills and get hands-on with current AI tools i
 n music production and learn about the history\, copyright and ethics of g
 enerative music. For more information and a full list of programs\, visit\
 ntpl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a201c84dacf581ff7e6743
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "https://elmocambo.com/event/the-yacht-rock-show/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Yacht Rock Show Celebration
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260516T193000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260516T193000
UID:cb1511fd75b621bcf7a90bf8c714fed9@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Yacht Rock Show Canada is an authentic tribute to the 70s 
 and 80s Classic Smooth Rock Era that defined a generation.\n\n Experience 
 an unforgettable musical voyage\, dancing and listening to classic hits fr
 om artists including: Toto\, Styx\, The Doobie Brothers\, Michael McDonald
 \, Christopher Cross\, Kenny Loggins\, Steely Dan\, Boz Scaggs\, Player\, 
 Little River Band\, Ambrosia.\n\nThe El Mocambo is a legendary live music 
 and entertainment venue in Toronto\, Canada\, that has hosted countless wo
 rld-famous artists since it opened in 1948\, including The Rolling Stones\
 , Elvis Costello\, Blondie\, The Ramones\, and Stevie Ray Vaughan. The new
  El Mocambo features state-of-the-art sound and lighting\, a recording stu
 dio\, and multiple floors for events and performances\, offering a modern\
 , VIP live music experience while maintaining its historical significance.
 \nCategories: Live Performances\, Music\, Nightlife\nPrice: 49.00
LOCATION:The El Mocambo\, 464 Spadina Ave\, Toronto\, ON\, M5T 2G8
URL:https://elmocambo.com/event/the-yacht-rock-show/
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
