SUMMARY:Penderecki Quartet 40th Anniversary Concert
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260521T183000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00";VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260521T183000
UID:ebcd10849a89a8216e0e12d214cb3852@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Their journey began in Poland\, where they won the prestigious
  Penderecki Prize at the 1986 National Chamber Music Competition in Łód
 ź. \n\nSince 1991\, they have served as Quartet-in-Residence at Wilfrid L
 aurier University\, helping shape one of Canada’s premier string program
 s. Known for their dedication to contemporary music\, the Penderecki’s h
 ave commissioned and performed over 100 new works. \n\nWe invite you to en
 joy their program of Krzysztof Penderecki: String Quartet No. 3 Leaves of 
 an Unwritten Diary and Franz Schubert: Quintet in C major for Two Cellos\,
  D. 956.\n\nArrive early to enjoy a pre-concert performance by Jacques For
 estier\, violin. \nCategories: Cultural\, Live Performances\, Music
LOCATION:Jane Mallett Theatre\, St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts\, 27 Fron
 t St E\, Toronto\, ON\, M5E 1B4
URL:https://musictorontoconcerts.com/concerts/penderecki-quartet
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
